    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2DYU7KiCLiPEkFZ1XxgUh76)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Independent: no other open PR touches the `sp-bibtex-lint` code of `sp-bibprocess` / `sp-academic.org`.\n- #474 changes `sp-litnotes-meta-fill`; either order works, the two do not share code.\n\n## What and why\n\n- A child BibTeX entry with `crossref = {parent}` now gets the fields it lacks from the parent, so `sp-litnotes-meta-fill` and the litnote autofill (pub-author / pub-editor / pub-title / pub-year) find `year`, `booktitle`, `publisher`, `editor`... in the child itself.\n- It is a new `crossref` kind of `sp-bibtex-lint`, built on the same machinery as the other fixes.\n\n## Commands\n\n- `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-crossref-entry`: the entry at point; lists what it would add and asks first; `C-u` is a dry run; one undo step.\n- `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-crossref-dryrun`: report for the whole file; writes nothing.\n- `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-crossref`: whole file after one question and a backup, like `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-files`.\n- The full `sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` report has a section and a button; `sp-bibtex-lint-convert` has an entry.\n- The buffer-wide commands are `sp-async-work` jobs: parents are indexed first in slices, and `M-x sp-batch-cancel` (#468) stops them; the report uses the echo-area hints of #470.\n- No key binding was added (the leader keys are being redesigned); say if you want one.\n\n## Rules\n\n- A field is added only when the child lacks it and the parent has it (non-empty); nothing is overwritten.\n- `sp-bibtex-crossref-fields`: groups of equivalent names (`year`/`date`/`month`, `location`/`address`), plus `publisher series volume number edition isbn editor organization eventtitle venue`. A child with its own `year` or `date` gets no `month`.\n- `sp-bibtex-crossref-renames`: type-aware renames, first rule wins:\n  - mv* parent: `title` → `maintitle`, `subtitle` → `mainsubtitle`, `titleaddon` → `maintitleaddon`\n  - `inbook` / `incollection` / `inproceedings` / `conference` / ...: `title` → `booktitle`, `subtitle` → `booksubtitle`, `titleaddon` → `booktitleaddon`\n  - `inbook` / `bookinbook` / `suppbook`: `author` → `bookauthor`\n  - `@periodical` parent, `@article` child: `title` → `journaltitle`, `subtitle` → `journalsubtitle`\n- `pages`, `doi`, `url`, `file`, `keywords`, `abstract`, `note`, `author` and `title` are never copied under their own name.\n- New fields are appended after the last field; `sp-bibtex-lint-fix-order` puts them in place. An entry laid out like `bibtex-mode` stays so.\n- Documented, bullet-pointed, in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (\"Fields from the crossref parent\"); `sp-bibprocess.el` is tangled from it (`tools/check-tangle.sh` passes).\n\n## Not done / limits\n\n- A parent's own parent is not followed (reported); a run does not see its own changes, so in a chain the second run passes the fields on.\n- `xref` is not used (biblatex does not inherit from it).\n- The default field list and renames follow my recollection of the biblatex manual's default inheritance setup; I could not open the manual from the cloud container, so please compare them with section 3.15.3 of the manual.\n\n## Tests\n\n- 12 new ERT tests with sample entries in `tests/sp-bibprocess-lint-test.el` (inproceedings/proceedings, inbook/book, book/mvbook, article/periodical, never overwrites, parent in another file, missing parent, apply + backup + second run, declined, dry-run report, full lint report, custom field and rename lists, entry command). The whole file runs: 73/73 in Emacs 29.3 batch.\n- Not tested: on the real `.bib` files (about 1300 entries), in a GUI Emacs 31, the report buttons by hand, or with the real litnote autofill afterwards.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-crossref-dryrun` on your main `.bib` file: the report opens, lists entries with the fields they would get, and does not change the file\n- [ ] The report lists a crossref key that does not exist as a problem, and shows a note for a parent with a crossref of its own\n- [ ] In a `.bib` buffer with point in an `@inproceedings` that has `crossref`, `C-u M-x sp-bibtex-lint-crossref-entry` only prints what it would add\n- [ ] Same without `C-u`: answer `n` (nothing changes), then `y` (fields added, one `C-/` undoes it)\n- [ ] An entry that already has `publisher`, `year` or `booktitle` keeps its own values\n- [ ] `inbook` child of a `@book`: gets `booktitle`, `bookauthor`, `year`, `publisher`; not `author`, `pages` or `doi`\n- [ ] `@article` child of a `@periodical`: gets `journaltitle`\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-crossref` asks once, writes a backup copy in `sp-bibtex-lint-backup-directory`, and the `.bib` file diff shows only added lines\n- [ ] A second `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-fix-crossref` finds nothing more (apart from chains)\n- [ ] `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-dryrun` shows the new \"fields from the crossref parent\" button and section; `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-convert` lists the new fix\n- [ ] `M-x sp-batch-cancel` stops the job while it indexes a big library\n- [ ] After the fix, `M-x sp-litnotes-meta-fill` on a litnote of a child entry fills `pub-year` and `pub-editor`\n- [ ] Parent in a different registered `.bib` file is found\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDVJ3YPpntR9CMdUMJ)_",
